# AINumbers pinned trust policy for rekor.sigstore.dev, per C2SP tlog-policy.md
# grammar. Rekor's current trust model is a single log with no witness
# cosigning, which tlog-policy.md permits via a bare "quorum none" line
# ("A policy without witness cosigning can be defined using a quorum none
# line"). Materialized by C2SP-TLOG-POLICY-FILE-1 from the pinned key already
# hardcoded in scripts/register-rekor.mjs (REKOR_PUBLIC_KEY_PEM/REKOR_LOG_ID),
# re-derivable via: GET https://rekor.sigstore.dev/api/v1/log/publicKey.
#
# KNOWN, NAMED DEVIATION from tlog-policy.md's vkey format (type byte +
# key-name hash, per signed-note.md's verifier-keys section): the key below
# is stored as bare hex of the log's SPKI DER bytes (ECDSA P-256), not a
# wrapped vkey. tlog-policy.md's vkey wrapping is defined for signed-note
# key types (Ed25519 is the common case); Rekor's checkpoint cosignature
# uses ECDSA P-256 with a 4-byte key-ID hint scheme of its own
# (register-rekor.mjs's verifyCheckpoint), which does not map onto the
# vkey construction without a second, Rekor-specific encoding step. Judged
# out of proportion for a single pinned instance — see
# scripts/register-rekor.test.mjs for the byte-identity check against the
# live REKOR_PUBLIC_KEY_PEM/REKOR_LOG_ID constants this file mirrors.
